{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:PredictedSpectra.SpectrahedralPhaseCollapse","@type":"LeanModule","name":"PredictedSpectra.SpectrahedralPhaseCollapse","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Determinant.Basic","lean:module:QOU.Interactions.GramMatrixH3Symbolic"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.lepton_unconditional_stability","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.lepton_unconditional_stability","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/spectrahedral-phase-collapse.lean#L79-L86","doc":"The unconditional stability of leptons. 1D abelian braid representations\n(electrons, neutrinos) project into the 1-dimensional Wedderburn channels, whose\ntraces scale as `q^n` and are therefore strictly positive for `q > 1` — so their\nGram matrices stay positive-definite across the whole `q > 1` regime. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.hadronic_melt_at_supergolden","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.hadronic_melt_at_supergolden","kind":"theorem","line":30,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/spectrahedral-phase-collapse.lean#L30-L69","doc":"The hadronic melt at the supergolden ratio.\nWe assert that for `q > ψ` (where `ψ` is the Supergolden Ratio), the `H_3(q)` Gram matrix\ndeterminant for the `(2,1)` representation is strictly negative, rendering the SDP formally infeasible.\n","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.spectrahedral_phase_collapse","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.spectrahedral_phase_collapse","kind":"theorem","line":13,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/spectrahedral-phase-collapse.lean#L13-L28","doc":"The Gram matrix rank-drop during aeon initiation at the inverse supergolden ratio.\nAt the threshold `u^3 + u - 1 = 0` (where `u = 1/ψ` and `ψ` is the Supergolden Ratio,\nthe first of the super metallic means), the Gram matrix of the Frobenius bilinear form\ndevelops a kernel and structurally drops rank (det(G) = 0). This geometrically collapses\nthe valid solution space onto a strictly lower-dimensional face of the spectrahedron.\n","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:spectrahedral-phase-collapse","label":"prop:spectrahedral-phase-collapse","md":"quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/spectrahedral-phase-collapse.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}